{"results":[{"url":"https://www.billboard.com/music/rock/jon-bon-jovi-madison-square-garden-concert-illness-1236302176/","final_url":"https://www.billboard.com/music/rock/jon-bon-jovi-madison-square-garden-concert-illness-1236302176/","title":"Jon Bon Jovi Cuts Short Madison Square Garden Concert Due to Illness","description":"Bon Jovi cut short their set at Madison Square Garden, as the rockers' singer Jon Bon Jovi struggled with the effects of a sinus infection.","language":"en","text":"Bon Jovi and Phil X perform onstage at the Forever Tour Kick Off - New York at Madison Square Garden on July 07, 2026 in New York City.\nTheo Wargo/Getty Images for Bon Jovi\n\nEspañol\n\nBon Jovi’s New York fans were left wanting more when frontman Jon Bon Jovi ended the show early on Thursday, July 23, due to illness.\n\nThe Rock & Roll Hall of Fame-inducted band cut short their set at Madison Square Garden, the eighth in a nine-show stand, as the singer struggled with the effects of a sinus infection.\n\n“Jon Bon Jovi spoke from stage and told fans he has been battling a sinus infection which led to the show’s early ending,” a rep for Bon Jovi tells *People*. “As part of the Bon Jovi residency at Madison Square Garden, Jon has said numerous times that it has been a joy to return to live shows for the band. Updated information will be available shortly.”\n\n### Explore\n\n### Bon Jovi\n\nSee latest videos, charts and news\n\nAccording to reports, Bon Jovi completed 90 minutes of a set that featured a guest performance by Train’s Pat Monahan, who joined in for a version of the *Slippery When Wet* hit from 1986, “Livin’ On a Prayer.”\n\nThe dates are part of the band’s *Forever Tour*, presented by Live Nation, which represents a return to the road after Jon Bon Jovi underwent reconstructive surgery on his vocal cords and then a years-long rehabilitative process.\n\n“Don’t throw away your ticket stubs I’m going to figure something out okay, don’t [fear],” Bon Jovi told the Garden, *People* reports. “Just hang onto it, I’m going to figure out how to reschedule.”\n\n“I’m gonna have to cool it for a night,” he added, prior to exiting the stage. “I feel great, I’ll see you again soon, bye bye.”\n\nBon Jovi’s MSG run is scheduled to wrap this Sunday, July 26, after which time the band crosses the Atlantic for five stadium shows in Scotland, the Republic of Ireland and England, the final of which is booked for Sept. 9 at London’s Wembley Stadium, the last of three concerts at the venue.\n\nJon Bovi has been candid about his recovery, saying the band assembled every month to rehearse to gauge his progress, but that until he felt he could confidently sing through a two-and-a-half-hour show, they weren’t hitting the road.“Day to day, I’m working hard on it,” he told *Entertainment Tonight* in 2024. “Nothing else matters until I work on getting better. It’s up to God at this point. I’ve done everything I can do. I won’t fake it … the legacy matters too much.”\n\n> View this post on Instagram\n\n## 1 Comment\n\nComments are moderated. They may be edited for clarity and reprinted\nin whole or in part in Billboard publications.\n\n### Leave a Comment\n\nDavid\n\nJuly 24, 2026 at 3:41 pm\n\nSorry but his lyrics are just a bunch of cliches strung together.","author":"Lars Brandle","published_date":"2026-07-24T05:42:24+00:00","latency_ms":1111.1852820031345,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}